DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The aarrccooffii driver supports the HP “Audio1” audio devices, based upon the
     Siemens PSB2160 “ARCOFI” codec, to implement the audio device interface
     described in audio(4).

     This device is found onboard HP 9000 workstations models 425e, 705 and
     710.

     The aarrccooffii is limited to a mono, 8000 KHz sound, either with 8-bit phone-
     quality mu-law or a-law samples, or 16-bit signed linear samples in big-
     endian byte order.

   AAUUDDIIOOCCTTLL SSEETTTTIINNGGSS
     The following encodings are supported:

           AUDIO_ENCODING_ULAW
           AUDIO_ENCODING_ALAW
           AUDIO_ENCODING_SLINEAR_BE  Natively supported.

           AUDIO_ENCODING_SLINEAR     Software converted to
                                      AUDIO_ENCODING_ULAW encoding.

           AUDIO_ENCODING_SLINEAR_LE
           AUDIO_ENCODING_ULINEAR_LE
           AUDIO_ENCODING_ULINEAR_BE  Software converted to
                                      AUDIO_ENCODING_SLINEAR_BE encoding.

   MMIIXXEERRCCTTLL SSEETTTTIINNGGSS
     The aarrccooffii has three audio ports:

           iinnppuuttss..lliinnee      The ‘line in’ jack connector.
           oouuttppuuttss..lliinnee     The ‘line out’ jack connector.
           oouuttppuuttss..ssppkkrr     The built-in speaker.

     Each port has a volume control, and can be muted.

     The oouuttppuuttss..lliinnee and oouuttppuuttss..ssppkkrr volume settings are tied to the same
     hardware setting.

